{"title":"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangle whose side lengths are whole numbers has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/8/bf8694fc22713935856ba05d14ce7bdfb4c5d924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cm^2$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />. The perimeter of this rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/a/78a062be13e0072c02c42485a60495462f146459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cm$\" width=\"23\" height=\"8\" />. Measured in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/a/78a062be13e0072c02c42485a60495462f146459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cm$\" width=\"23\" height=\"8\" />, the positive difference between the length and width of the rectangle is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d2cde007e814ac2ffcd4cc2d07835c4c7b970a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 47 \\quad \\text{(B) } 2 \\quad \\text{(C) } 22 \\quad \\text{(D) } 8 \\quad \\text{(E) } 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"293\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use factors to solve this based on the area. The factors of 48 are \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/4/fe495a278ed85b295d294f955c4c251a3a9c9a4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 24, 48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"199\" height=\"16\" />. Since the perimeter is 32, the two \nfactors of 48 have to add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/930177992b542a2c141d6753555826b66b41a557.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32/2 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />. The only factors that meet \nthis criteria are 12 and 4. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7c671a7dd22ce72e6d58a581d5d498c8e7566b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 - 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> which \nequals to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e81ca9c5c8715be868438500743202d6773d05bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Anewmathday\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.